Spec: Feature UploadManager Security Hardening (2.2 / SEC-02 & SEC-04)

Purpose:
  Prevent unnecessary retention of plaintext passwords in RAM, guard against unencrypted remote HTTP credential transmission, and sanitize multipart Content-Disposition filenames in UploadManager.

Platform: C++26 (Linux) / C++23 (Windows, macOS), Qt6

References:
  ../../../desktop-gallery.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /include/UploadManager.hpp
  /src/UploadManager.cpp
  /src/MainWindow.cpp
  /data/Prioritaetenliste.md

Must:
  Remove m_lastUser and m_lastPass from UploadManager so user passwords are not kept in memory beyond the login request serialization.
  Sanitize filenames in Content-Disposition multipart headers by stripping quotes, backslashes, CR, and LF characters.
  Warn the user and require explicit confirmation before logging in to a non-localhost server over unencrypted HTTP.

Must not:
  Persist or retain plaintext passwords in UploadManager member variables.
  Insert unsanitized filenames containing quotes or control characters into HTTP multipart headers.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Remove m_lastUser and m_lastPass from include/UploadManager.hpp and src/UploadManager.cpp.
  [x] #2 Sanitize Content-Disposition filename in src/UploadManager.cpp and add non-localhost HTTP warning in src/MainWindow.cpp.
  [x] #3 Verify compilation via cmake --build build and mark item 2.2 as completed in data/Prioritaetenliste.md.

Done when:
  cmake --build build succeeds without errors and UploadManager no longer stores plaintext passwords or allows header injection via filenames.
